{"name":"Stromboli","hex":"#406356","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Stromboli","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["One of the Aeolian Islands in the Tyrrhenian Sea; it has an active volcano"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Stromboli"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stromboli","blocks":[{"text":"Stromboli is an island in the Tyrrhenian Sea, off the north coast of Sicily, containing Mount Stromboli, one of the four active volcanoes in Italy. It is one of the seven Aeolian Islands, a volcanic arc north of Sicily, and the mythological home of Aeolus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Aerial_image_of_Stromboli_%28view_from_the_northeast%29.jpg/330px-Aerial_image_of_Stromboli_%28view_from_the_northeast%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stromboli"},{"title":"Stromboli (1950 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Stromboli (Italian: Stromboli (Terra di Dio), lit. 'Stromboli (Land of God)') is a 1950 drama film directed by Roberto Rossellini and starring Ingrid Bergman. The film is considered a classic example of Italian neorealism."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/49/Stromboli_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stromboli_(1950_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/DenglerSW-Stromboli-20040928-1230x800.jpg/500px-DenglerSW-Stromboli-20040928-1230x800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/DenglerSW-Stromboli-20040928-1230x800.jpg/500px-DenglerSW-Stromboli-20040928-1230x800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"September 2004 Stromboli eruption","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADenglerSW-Stromboli-20040928-1230x8